                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "OS chrome and safe areas",
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "bold"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "OmAHW",
                  "name": "OS chrome and safe areas content",
                  "fill": "#4E5D4D",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "iOS STATUS BAR\nOS owns time, network and battery. Respect safe area and Dynamic Island geometry.\n\nANDROID STATUS BAR\nOS owns status icons. Respect system-bar and display-cutout insets.\n\nBOTTOM SYSTEM AREA\nHome indicator / gesture or 3-button navigation stay OS-owned. Never draw replicas.\n\nKEYBOARD\nInsets are dynamic. Keep focused field and key action visible; do not hard-code height.",
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "lsu1L",
              "name": "Test viewport matrix",
              "width": 250,
              "height": "fill_container",
              "fill": "#FFFFFF",
              "cornerRadius": 8,
              "stroke": "#C5CEBF",
              "strokeWidth": 1,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 12,
              "padding": 16,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "N4158M",
                  "name": "Test viewport matrix heading",
                  "fill": "#1F2B21",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Test viewport matrix",
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "bold"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "g74df",
                  "name": "Test viewport matrix content",
                  "fill": "#4E5D4D",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "COMPACT PHONE\n320 × 640\nWrapped product titles, prices, narrow forms, keyboard overlap.\n\nCOMMON PHONE\n390 × 844\nPrimary buyer and seller flow canvas.\n\nLARGE PHONE\n430 × 932\nCheck line length, reach and card stretch.\n\nTABLET / SPLIT\n768 × 1024 + resized narrow window.\n\nADMIN\n1280 × 800 / 1440 × 900; mobile fallback 390 × 844.\n\nReview canvases only; support floors remain undecided.",
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "NbXrr",
              "name": "Adaptive behavior",
              "width": 250,
              "height": "fill_container",
              "fill": "#FFFFFF",
              "cornerRadius": 8,
              "stroke": "#C5CEBF",
              "strokeWidth": 1,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 12,
              "padding": 16,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "B0CtbN",
                  "name": "Adaptive behavior heading",
                  "fill": "#1F2B21",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Adaptive behavior",
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "bold"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Fn3dD",
                  "name": "Adaptive behavior content",
                  "fill": "#4E5D4D",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "ONE COLUMN FIRST\nBuyer and seller tasks remain readable and vertically scrollable. No horizontal scrolling for core tasks.\n\nUSE AVAILABLE WINDOW\nRespond to current width, height and insets, not device label alone.\n\nLARGE WINDOWS\nAdd panes or columns only when they aid the task; retain a usable single-column fallback.\n\nRESIZE AND ROTATE\nPreserve form values and current task; let content reflow.",
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "eCli6",
              "name": "Inputs and accessibility",
              "width": 250,
              "height": "fill_container",
              "fill": "#FFFFFF",
              "cornerRadius": 8,
              "stroke": "#C5CEBF",
              "strokeWidth": 1,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 12,
              "padding": 16,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "d43dD6",
                  "name": "Inputs and accessibility heading",
                  "fill": "#1F2B21",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Inputs and accessibility",
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "bold"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Zu1if",
                  "name": "Inputs and accessibility content",
                  "fill": "#4E5D4D",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "MINIMUM HIT AREAS\niOS: 44 × 44 pt.\nAndroid: 48 × 48 dp.\nExpand invisible hit areas when safe.\n\nTEXT SCALING\nRespect system text-size settings. Reflow rather than truncate.\n\nGESTURES\nVisible controls remain available; custom gestures are never the only route.\n\nKEYBOARD AND POINTER\nVisible focus, pressed and disabled states; keep validation and next action accessible.",
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "QaOtx",
              "name": "Connectivity and interruptions",
              "width": 250,
              "height": "fill_container",
              "fill": "#FFFFFF",
